---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { CONTACT, ACTIVE_ADDRESS, ADDRESS } from '../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Our funeral home', url: '/our-funeral-home/' }];
---

<Page
  title="Our Funeral Home in Dunbar — Countess Crescent"
  heading="Our funeral home"
  description="Our funeral home in Dunbar: where to find us, parking, accessibility, and what to expect when you visit. Moving to Countess Crescent, Dunbar."
  standfirst="A quiet place to sit, whether you are arranging something or simply want to spend time with someone."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  {
    !ADDRESS.moveComplete && (
      <Callout tone="accent" title="We are moving to Countess Crescent">
        <p>
          We are moving to new premises on Countess Crescent, Dunbar. Our telephone
          number, our team and the way we work are all staying exactly the same — only
          the address is changing.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Until the move is complete you will find us at {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.street},{' '}
          {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.locality} {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.postcode}. If you are unsure where to
          come, telephone{' '}
          <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a> and we
          will tell you.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    )
  }

  <h2>Where to find us</h2>
  <p>
    <address class="not-italic">
      <strong>John Bald Funeral Directors</strong><br />
      {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.street}<br />
      {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.locality}, {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.region}<br />
      {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.postcode}
    </address>
  </p>
  <p>
    Telephone <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a><br />
    Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Coming to see us</h2>
  <p>
    You do not need an appointment to call in and ask a question. Plenty of people put
    their head round the door to ask about a funeral plan, or to record what they would
    like for themselves, or simply because they have been meaning to for months. The
    kettle is always on.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are coming to arrange a funeral, or to spend time with someone in our care,
    telephone first so we can make sure the room is free and that you are not disturbed.
  </p>

  <h2>Visiting someone in our care</h2>
  <p>
    Whenever you would like, for as long as you would like — including evenings and
    weekends. There is no limit on how many times you come. Children are welcome if you
    feel it would help them, and we will talk you through what to expect beforehand.
  </p>

  <h2>Services here</h2>
  <p>
    We can hold a short service at the funeral home for a small gathering. For some
    families it is exactly right — quieter than a church, warmer than a crematorium
    chapel, and no travelling. Ask us if you would like to see the room.
  </p>

  <h2>Parking and access</h2>
  <p>
    There is parking at the funeral home, and the building is accessible at ground level.
    If anyone in your family has particular needs — mobility, a wheelchair, a hearing
    loop, or simply somewhere quiet to sit away from other people — tell us in advance
    and we will have it ready.
  </p>

  <h2>Next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/arranging-a-funeral/">Arranging a funeral</a></li>
    <li><a href="/contact/">Contact us</a></li>
    <li><a href="/about/">About John Bald Funeral Directors</a></li>
  </ul>
</Page>

<!--
  Before launch: confirm the Countess Crescent street number, postcode and parking
  arrangements, then update src/data/site.ts and set ADDRESS.moveComplete to true.
  That one change updates the address across every page, the footer and the
  FuneralHome schema.
-->

